  "narration": {
    "title": "Atlanta Sweeps Its Way Into the Top Three",
    "intro": "The Braves went 6-0 this week and jumped six spots to third in the power ranking. Nobody else near the top moved much, but Atlanta didn't leave a choice.",
    "power_lead": "Milwaukee stays first at 85-51, Christian Yelich going 9-for-16 to keep the engine humming. The real climb belongs to Atlanta, a perfect 6-0 with a Chris Sale nine-inning shutout in the middle of it, and to Tampa Bay, up six to sixth on a 5-1 week behind Junior Caminero.",
    "offense_lead": "The Cubs still own the best team OPS at .767, a hair ahead of the Dodgers at .757. Washington sits third at .755, quietly one of the more productive lineups in the league.",
    "staffs_lead": "The Yankees have the best rotation ERA at 3.34, with Detroit (3.42) and Milwaukee (3.43) right behind. Boston's bullpen leads the relief board at 2.94, so the Red Sox and Yankees are covering both ends of the game about as well as anyone."
  }
